From: Coram Engineering <eng@coram.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] fmp4mux: backport upstream chunk-mode drain fixes

Backport of three upstream fixes onto gst-plugins-rs c3740cd6a. Together they
fix a permanent isofmp4mux stall in chunk mode: once a GOP starts after the
current fragment end, the drain produces nothing on every aggregate call, no
chunk or fragment is started, nothing is pushed downstream and the input queue
grows without bound. The streamer does not crash and no alert fires.

Reproduced on a live H.264 + AAC pipeline (fragment-duration=2s,
chunk-duration=100ms) where a GOP began 36.76us after the fragment end: 373
drains entered in 60s, 385 AGGREGATOR_FLOW_NEED_DATA returns, zero chunks and
zero fragments started, 3m03s of GOPs queued and still growing.

Upstream commits, applied to the pre-rename path (mux/fmp4/... rather than
mux/isobmff/...) since this revision predates the mp4/fmp4 plugin de-duplication:

  c64db4e0d  fmp4mux: Fix draining in chunk mode after partial GOPs were drained
             The keyframe check was inverted, so GOPs starting *on* a keyframe
             were wrongly marked as late. Applied to the single occurrence that
             exists at this revision; upstream has a second one added later.

  6bdeecf1d  fmp4mux: Fix late GOP handling
             A late GOP must not skip the drain entirely -- there may still be
             data to output.

  a06e4abb5  isobmff/fmp4mux: Fix delayed push when GOPs start after fragment end
             With fragment_filled set, dequeue_end_pts is pinned to
             fragment_end_pts; if all remaining GOPs start past it the drain
             loop breaks with nothing dequeued. Reset fragment_filled so the
             drain falls back to chunk boundaries and can make progress.

Not backported: 78dfb9302 ("Fix fragment / chunk decision for
chunk-mode=keyframe"). It targets the key-frame chunk mode added after this
revision, which does not exist here, and restructures shared fill-check logic.

These fixes are only available upstream on revisions requiring gstreamer-rs
0.25+/gstreamer 1.28+, so bumping the wrap is not an option while we build
gstreamer 1.23.1.
--- a/mux/fmp4/src/fmp4mux/imp.rs
+++ b/mux/fmp4/src/fmp4mux/imp.rs
@@ -1620,7 +1620,7 @@
                     // previously drained a partial GOP because the GOP is ending too far after the
                     // planned fragment end.
                     if gop.start_pts > fragment_end_pts
-                        && !gop.buffers.first().is_some_and(|b| {
+                        && gop.buffers.first().is_some_and(|b| {
                             b.buffer.flags().contains(gst::BufferFlags::DELTA_UNIT)
                         })
                     {
@@ -1980,9 +1980,9 @@
                 || settings.manual_split
         );
 
+        stream.late_gop = false;
         let mut gops = Vec::with_capacity(stream.queued_gops.len());
-        if stream.queued_gops.is_empty() || stream.late_gop {
-            stream.late_gop = false;
+        if stream.queued_gops.is_empty() {
             return Ok(gops);
         }
 
@@ -2119,6 +2119,27 @@
         if let Some(chunk_duration) = settings.chunk_duration {
             // Chunk mode
 
+            // Check if the oldest queued GOP starts at or after fragment end
+            // PTS. If fragment_filled is true but all remaining data starts
+            // past the fragment end, this stream has no data within this
+            // fragment. Fall through to chunk boundaries to avoid stalling
+            // the drain.
+            let mut fragment_filled = fragment_filled;
+            if fragment_filled
+                && stream
+                    .queued_gops
+                    .back()
+                    .is_some_and(|gop| gop.start_pts >= fragment_end_pts)
+            {
+                gst::trace!(
+                    CAT,
+                    obj = stream.sinkpad,
+                    "Fragment filled but GOP starts after fragment end PTS {}, falling through to chunk boundaries",
+                    fragment_end_pts,
+                );
+                fragment_filled = false;
+            }
+
             let dequeue_end_pts = if let Some(chunk_end_pts) = chunk_end_pts {
                 // Not the first stream
                 chunk_end_pts
